# netsurf: a child-list change among more than blocks builds the parent again whole (patch 467)
# Generated 2026-11-27
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 466)
#
# 380's block placement (html_rl_block_change) tracks the parent's child
# boxes as blocks, floats, inline content, flex, grid and table boxes; any
# other child box -- wpblog's anonymous table (type 3, the wrapper box
# normalisation makes around a display: table-cell child among blocks) --
# declined into the full rebuild ("parent holds more than blocks", 1.0 a
# load). The box-level reason 460 answers for a restyle: the decline now
# goes to decline:, where the parent block, if a plain block, is built
# again whole (440) from the DOM -- every child made afresh, the page laid
# out whole -- with that rebuild's own checks deciding, as 446 (sibling
# risk) and 454 (removed objects) do. The child's box type is logged.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c
@@ -9790,6 +9790,9 @@
 	const char *why = NULL;
